cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Titra or its evaluation, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Titra: Open oxygen control for preterm babies on low-cost CPAP"
abstract: >-
  An oxygen controller for preterm babies on CPAP, built on QNX 8.0, that holds SpO2 in the 91-95% target range and
  puts each cot in a defined safe state when a sensor, a cable or a piece of its own software fails. The repository
  holds the deterministic C core, the QNX processes and image, a simulated preterm baby, oximeter and blender, the
  closed-loop and step-test evaluation, an on-board advisor with a looped language model as a QNX resource manager, and a
  fault matrix measured on the host clock against the QNX guest.
authors:
  - family-names: Donovici
    given-names: Marc
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Marc-Dvci/Titra"
keywords:
  - "neonatal oxygen"
  - "closed-loop control"
  - "preterm infants"
  - "CPAP"
  - "QNX"
  - "real-time"
  - "fault containment"
  - "medical devices"
